  "response_text": "At entry, PendSV_Handler reads the process stack pointer (PSP) to establish the current thread\u2019s stack location, then calls osSched to decide which thread should run next. It pushes the callee-saved registers (R4\u2013R11) onto the current thread\u2019s stack, stores the updated PSP value into that thread\u2019s control block, and loads the PSP value from the chosen thread\u2019s control block. Finally, it pops R4\u2013R11 from the new thread\u2019s stack and executes BX LR to return from the exception, resuming the new thread exactly where it left off.\\n",
